1. length()
• Purpose: Returns the total number of characters in a string.
eg: String s = "Java";
    System.out.println(s.length());

2. charAt()
• Purpose: Returns the single character located at a specified index position.
  eg: String s = "Java";
      System.out.println(s.charAt(1));

3. toUpperCase()
• Purpose: Converts all characters in a string into uppercase letters.
  eg: String s = "java";
      System.out.println(s.toUpperCase());


6. equalsIgnoreCase()

Compares Strings without considering uppercase or lowercase differences.

